# confluid: validation policies, and the variables a config references as ${env:NAME} (docs/interpolation.md)

# -- Validation (docs/validation.md)
# CONFLUID_VALIDATE_INIT=strict   strict | warn | off — validation of direct Python Cls(...) calls
# CONFLUID_VALIDATE_YAML=strict   strict | warn | off — validation when a YAML config materializes its objects
# CONFLUID_VALIDATE_TOOL=strict   strict | warn | off — validation at a tool entry (an MCP tool, a CLI)

# -- Workspace paths a config may reference
# DATA_ROOT=/path/to/datasets   folder of the datasets; configs write ${env:DATA_ROOT}/... (docs/interpolation.md)

# not for .env: CONFLUID_BENCH_PROFILE — set for one run of examples/performance.py to profile it
# not for .env: EXAMPLE_DATA_ROOT LIFECYCLE_ROOT — set by the examples themselves to demonstrate ${env:...}
# not for .env: XDG_CONFIG_HOME XDG_CONFIG_DIRS — set by the desktop session; the search path for user-level config files
# not for .env: COMP_WORDS — set by the shell while it completes
